# ─── Server ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PORT=3001

# ─── LLM Provider — choose ONE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Option A: Google Gemini (cloud — recommended for first-time setup)
# Get a free key at https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
# Then paste it into the app Settings panel, or set it here:
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# Option B: Ollama (fully local — no API key required)
# 1. Install Ollama: https://ollama.ai
# 2. Pull a model: ollama pull qwen2.5-coder   (or llama3.2, codellama, etc.)
# 3. Switch to "Ollama" in the in-app Settings panel — no .env change needed.
#    The base URL and model are saved to localStorage automatically.
#
# Optional overrides (defaults shown):
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
# OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen2.5-coder

# ─── Legacy CLI agents (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# The standalone agents in src/agents/ (npm run heal, npm run run:auto-pom, etc.)
# use Anthropic Claude by default via src/core/llm-client.ts.
# They will run in deterministic MOCK mode if this key is absent.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-your-key-here
